p('B3 was a floor-level beam in the previous model. Removing it is not deletion of the floor support: its job is transferred to the T-N truss lower chord through joist seats/connections that still need detailing. This comparison gives no new load credit to the existing north garage wall.')
table([['','One B2','Two beams'],['Positions north of south wall','161.375 in','130.833 and 191.917 in'],['Candidate interior rails','W8×31','W8×24 each'],['Longest joist span','91.625 in','61.083 in'],['Primary steel + 10% connection allowance',f"{single['steel_with_connections_lb']:,.0f} lb",f"{two['steel_with_connections_lb']:,.0f} lb"],['Maximum gravity screen ratio',f"{single['max_ratio']:.3f}",f"{two['max_ratio']:.3f}"],['Maximum global service movement',f"{single['max_vertical_in']:.3f} in",f"{two['max_vertical_in']:.3f} in"]],[232,150,150])
p('The single-beam option is about 355 lb lighter in primary steel. The two-beam option shortens the longest joist span by one third, which may allow shallower or lighter secondary floor framing. The 9 psf floor dead-load allowance is held constant in this study; secondary joist sizing/cost has not been optimized, so the whole-floor weight advantage is not settled.')
p('Several single-beam positions have the same minimum tested primary weight. The midpoint is preferred because it minimizes the longest joist span between fixed T1 and T-N supports, not because the steel search found a unique mathematical optimum. This is a finite position/section comparison with selected companion-member upsizing.')
p('Both arrangements retain the preceding T1 option: W6×16 lower chord, W6×20 upper chord, HSS 2×2×1/8 verticals and HSS 2½×2½×1/8 end diagonals. The 1,000 lb lifted trolley load and provisional dynamic/equipment allowances are retained. All columns and the west O3 transfer beam remain at their existing coordinates.')
story.append(PageBreak());h('Floor framing comparison');story.append(Image(str(P/'beam-position-comparison.png'),width=532,height=532*10/15));p('Arrows inside the deck indicate north-south floor-joist spanning direction. Dimension chains show support spans; they are not W-beam spans. Both W beams still span 224.25 inches east-west between T-W and T-E. The floor remains open south of y = 72 inches. The deck extends to y = 255 inches, giving a 2-inch north overhang past T-N at y = 253 inches.')
p('B2 no longer needs to line up with W3: it transfers through T-W, which connects to the unchanged O3/W3 support line at y = 185 inches. That indirect load path is included in the connected model; its joints and restraint must be designed. No extra columns or garage-floor footings have been added by this comparison.')
