p('The limits are the inherited 0.90 combined-force screening metric and 0.75-inch maximum absolute global service movement. “Meets” means only those conditional gravity screens. The 130-inch trial exceeds the arbitrary movement threshold by about 0.003 inch; this does not demonstrate that such a layout is physically impossible. Candidate families and connection assumptions materially affect the result.')
p('For each layout, the Python model regenerates member intersections and the floor tributary-load distribution. It removes B3 and places the north floor reactions on T-N, checks the selected frame, upsizes failing companion families where possible, and tests W-rail section combinations. Other truss members are held fixed except required upsizing; a simultaneous global reoptimization could change the ranking.')
p('There are six one-beam positions and three two-beam layouts. Rail candidates are actual catalogue W sections at or below 8 inches actual depth. Trolley loads are sampled at nine locations on each rail and on T1, one operating trolley at a time. The whole connected frame is solved for each option; no truss is assigned the entire building load independently.')
