p('The T-N lower chord can serve as the north floor collector in this conditional model. Its own bending, axial force and connection behavior still matter: being part of a truss does not make local floor-bearing effects disappear. The truss shares load through its upper chord, web system and supporting columns.')
p('The one-beam option has little room below the chosen 0.75-inch global movement target. That target is not a code-specific relative beam deflection or trolley alignment check. This result should guide layout selection, not final member purchase. Joist deflection, the separately discussed 1,000 lb concentrated floor item, trolley flange-local checks and floor vibration still need member-level design.')
p('Unchanged limitations: first-order analysis; assumed rigid joints and fixed bases; assumed chord brace spacing; simplified W torsion without restrained warping; unverified roof collectors and diaphragm action; no completed site wind/seismic, connection, anchor or footing design. North floor seating into T-N and T-W/O3 transfer details are especially important for this revision.')
p('Reproduction: run run_sweep.py with the FreeCAD Python environment or equivalent NumPy/SciPy runtime; the balanced single-beam case is generated with BEAM_YS=[161.375] and LAYOUT=single-161 via test_layout.py. The scripts depend on the preceding revision-4 selected-options.json. Full per-layout selections, member demands and column reactions are in results/. make_plans.py and report.py generate this comparison. The AISC/Atlas section data and load references are those documented in revision 3.')
